text:
hema: quick sync on transport + pagination retry tradeoffs across SDKs (py/ts/go). need a clear recommendation for: unary vs streaming control, resume-token semantics, and how retries interact with speculative prefetching.

joel: TL;DR proposal: use unary for single-call patterns + explicit Stream/Session object for long-lived flows. keep resume tokens opaque but stable across model variants.

anya: agree re: coarse split. add that resume tokens must be idempotent and include server-side monotonic offsets so retries are safe. otherwise we risk duplicate work on resume.

marco: implementation note for Go/TS: streaming control is heavier for browser TS (ws/fallback) and for users behind proxies. prefer optional Stream API rather than implicit streaming on every request.

lee: also think about retries: if client retries a paginated unary call and server has already advanced the continuation cursor, client should use resume token returned in 409-like error to continue rather than blind replay. propose error shape: { code: 409, reason: "stale_cursor", resume_token: "..." } so SDKs can auto-recover.

hema: good — combine that with a backoff policy: on retry, if we see stale_cursor -> perform a resume call with provided resume_token; only escalate to user after N attempts.

joel: ergonomics across languages: expose a high-level iterator that hides retries and resume internally. example surfaces:

// python
for page in client.list_responses(request):
    for item in page.items:
        process(item)
// ts
for await (const page of client.listResponses(request)) {
  page.items.forEach(handle)
}
// go
it := client.ListResponses(ctx, req)
for it.Next() {
  item := it.Value()
}

SDK handles stale_cursor and resume transparently. provide opt-in hooks for users to see telemetry.

anya: about speculative prefetch + pagination: if SDK prefetches the next page and the preceding call eventually fails, how do we avoid charging/wasting tokens? two parts: accounting and rollback. we should only bill generated tokens when the model emits tokens to the client; keep speculative work unbilled unless consumed. that requires server to tag token attribution in traces.

marco: on rollback: server should expose a cancel token endpoint for long-lived sessions to indicate speculative prefetched but unused contexts can be reclaimed. for unary flows this is tougher — but keeping window small reduces waste.

lee: for transport optimization: add a header flow for quick negotiation: `x-rw-session: opts=stream,prefetch=on,ver=1`. if SDK sees stream supported it can open a control stream; otherwise fallback to unary. this avoids double-prefetch with older servers.

hema: timeline decision: short-term (v1): unary default, opt-in Session/Stream API, resume-token errors with explicit resume_token field, iterator surfaces hide retries, default conservative prefetch window=96 tokens. long-term (v2): session control stream with push hints, server-side reclaim/cancel endpoint, unified cache/policy module in SDKs.

joel: tests: add cross-version e2e: old-sdk + new-server, new-sdk + old-server, and streaming enabled/disabled permutations. also simulate stale_cursor errors and assert iterator resumes without duplicate items.

anya: agree. i'll own telemetry spec: fields: `resume_attempts`, `stale_cursor=true/false`, `prefetch_window`, `transport_mode=unary|stream`.

marco: small API note for Go: iterator should expose `ResumeToken()` on error to let callers persist resume points if they want manual control. keep default high-level iterator auto-resume.

lee: add code sample for session API (pseudo):

// python
session = client.open_session(prefetch_stream=True)
for event in session.stream():
  if event.type == "prefetch_hint":
     session.adjust_window(event.window)

// ts
const s = client.session({prefetchStream:true})
s.on('prefetch_hint', (w) => s.adjustWindow(w))

hema: ok next steps: @anya draft telemetry + error shapes, @marco add resume-token plumbing to Go iterator, @joel update TS/python iterator docs + examples, @lee add header negotiation names. infra-bot: please create tracking issue.

infra-bot: created issue INFR-3012: "sdk-transport-pagination-retries-session-plan" assigned to @hema.

hema: thanks. i'll spin a short RFC and include the test matrix. re-open thread if anything else comes up. :handshake:
